#pragma once

// World Dungeon "System Carl" theme -- full 1-bit sprite set.
// Generated by Pixel, 2026-08-18. Supersedes sprites/world_dungeon_default_sprites.h
// and kThemeCarl in its entirety per parent ruling: one coherent art pass, one hand,
// one convention -- do not mix with the prior (unverified-polarity) set.
//
// Polarity verified from source, not by comparison to prior art (which was itself
// unverified): GameSprites.cpp drawSprite() decodes level = lsb | (msb<<1); level 0
// (both plane bits 0) always plots ink (kLevelThreshold[0]=16, i.e. every dither cell
// fires); level 3 (both bits 1) never plots. drawPixel(..., true) is confirmed Color::Black
// via GfxRenderer::drawPixelDither<Color::Black>. So: ink pixel -> bit 0 in both planes,
// blank pixel -> bit 1 in both planes. This header uses ONLY levels 0/3 (no dither cells
// ever partially fire), so LSB plane == MSB plane == "is this pixel blank" mask.
//
// 14x20 per sprite (GameRenderer.h CELL_W/CELL_H), stride=2. All 8 tiles, the player,
// all 21 monsters, all 23 items redrawn fresh -- none reused from the prior file.
// Plus one generic Companion sprite (fallback for Forge's in-flight pet system --
// see Phase 3 spec for the TileTheme field this slots into).
//
// Note: no local #include for Sprite2bpp.h here — GameTheme.h already
// includes it before this file, matching the prior sprites-header convention
// (see world_dungeon_default_sprites.h). A self-include here resolves
// incorrectly from the host-test include path (test/../src/game/../../sprites/).

